  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting Migrants&apos; Inclusion in T&#xfc;rkiye&#x2019;s Transition to a Green Economy</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The joint programme will contribute to the inclusion of migrants in the sustainable and green development of Turkey and its transition to a green and circular economy. Climate Change impacts, including displacement, are already being felt in Turkey today. T&#xfc;rkiye&apos;s Green Deal Action Plan stresses that economic growth needs to consider climate change. Turkey has committed to a &apos;just transition&apos; to a green economy and targets carbon neutrality by 2053. To ensure that the benefits of a &apos;just transition&apos; are shared and that no-one is left behind in that transition, migrant populations and the sectors that employ them, must be part of the process. &#xa0;The Joint Programme (JP) aims to ensure the inclusion of migrants and migrant-owned MSMEs in the sustainable and green development of T&#xfc;rkiye and its transition to a green and circular economy. It aims to support Migrant-owned and migrant employing startups and established MSMEs, including those established by women and youth entrepreneurs, adapt and innovate for circular economy and EU market access. It also aims to support them to build partnerships, access finance, and build peer links to grow their businesses.</narrative>
  </description>
